    "knowledge_point": "Differentiating Expressions Involving the Cosecant Function",
    "problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)={x}^{2}-6csc⁡x.$",
    "worked_solution": "We take the derivative of each term and then add them, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-6csc⁡x) \\\\  & =2x-6(-csc⁡xcot⁡x) \\\\  & =2x+6csc⁡xcot⁡x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
